# SHADE Reproducibility Guide

This document provides exact step-by-step instructions to reproduce every table
and figure in the paper. All results can be reproduced on a single GPU in
approximately 20 hours, or in parallel across multiple GPUs in 6–8 hours.

---

## Hardware Requirements

### Minimum (simulation experiments)
- CPU: 8+ cores
- RAM: 32 GB
- Storage: 50 GB (for datasets + checkpoints)
- GPU: NVIDIA GPU with 8 GB VRAM (optional but strongly recommended)

### Recommended
- CPU: 16+ cores
- RAM: 64 GB
- GPU: NVIDIA A100 / RTX 3090+ (24 GB VRAM)

### Physical Testbed (Section 6.6 / Table 4)
Requires the exact hardware listed in Table 3 of the paper:
- Class A: Raspberry Pi 4 Model B (4 GB)
- Class B: NVIDIA Jetson Orin NX 16 GB
- Class C: Dell PowerEdge R750 with NVIDIA A30
- Class D: AWS c5.4xlarge instance

Power measurement: TP-Link Tapo P115 (Classes A, B) + Dell iDRAC (Class C).

