## Step 1 — Environment Setup

```bash
git clone https://github.com/[username]/SHADE.git
cd SHADE
python -m venv shade_env && source shade_env/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
pip install -e .
```

Verify installation:
```bash
python -c "import shade; print('SHADE installed successfully')"
python -c "import torch; print(f'PyTorch {torch.__version__}, CUDA: {torch.cuda.is_available()}')"
```

---

## Step 2 — Download and Preprocess Datasets

### Synthetic-HET (generated locally, ~2 minutes)
```bash
python datasets/synthetic_het/generate.py \
    --n_nodes 500 \
    --n_tasks 10000 \
    --n_seeds 30 \
    --output data/synthetic_het/
```

### Google Cluster 2011 (~15 GB download, ~30 min preprocessing)
```bash
# Download (requires ~15 GB disk space)
bash scripts/download_datasets.sh --dataset google_cluster

# Preprocess to SHADE format (maps fields to τᵢ descriptor)
python datasets/google_cluster/preprocess.py \
    --input data/raw/google_cluster/ \
    --output data/processed/google_cluster/
```

### Azure Functions 2023 (~5 GB download, ~15 min preprocessing)
```bash
bash scripts/download_datasets.sh --dataset azure_functions

python datasets/azure_functions/preprocess.py \
    --input data/raw/azure_functions/ \
    --output data/processed/azure_functions/
```

