## Step 3 — Train SHADE (or Use Pretrained Weights)

### Option A: Use pretrained weights (recommended for evaluation)

Pre-trained weights are provided in `results/pretrained/`:
```
results/pretrained/
  shade_synthetic_het.pt     # Trained on Synthetic-HET (best of 30 trials)
  shade_google_cluster.pt    # Trained on Google Cluster
  shade_azure_functions.pt   # Trained on Azure Functions
```

### Option B: Train from scratch (30 trials × 50,000 steps each)

```bash
# Single trial (for testing)
python experiments/train_shade.py \
    --dataset synthetic_het \
    --n_nodes 500 \
    --seed 42 \
    --checkpoint_dir results/checkpoints/

# All 30 trials in parallel (requires 30 GPUs or sequential ~12 hours on 1 GPU)
bash scripts/run_training.sh --dataset synthetic_het --n_trials 30
```

